The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{x}{32}$ on $[0,8]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1, xmax=9.4, ymin=-0.04, ymax=0.35, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6,8}, ytick={0.1,0.2}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:8] {x/32};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the first quartile $Q_{1}$.

questions.solution_text:
$F(x)=\int_{0}^{x}\frac{t}{32}\,dt$
$=\frac{x^{2}}{64}$
$\frac{x^{2}}{64}=0.25$
$x^{2}=16$
$Q_{1}=4$
The root $x=-4$ is rejected because it lies outside $[0,8]$.
[tikz]
